'''Morokei''' is one of the eight high-ranking [[Skyrim:Dragon Priest|dragon priests]] of Skyrim. He is located in the antechamber of [[Skyrim:Labyrinthian|Labyrinthian]] and possesses both the [[Skyrim:Staff of Magnus|Staff of Magnus]] and his [[Skyrim:Morokei (item)|eponymous mask]].

As you journey through Labyrinthian, ghostly images from the past reveal that [[Skyrim:Savos Aren|Savos Aren]] had encountered Morokei prior to you. In an act of desperation, he sacrificed the lives of two [[SR:College of Winterhold (faction)|College]] students in order to keep Morokei sealed within Labyrinthian for the good of Skyrim. 

Throughout Labyrinthian, Morokei taunts you - at first, in the [[Lore:Dragon Language|dragon language]], then secondly in the Skyrim vernacular - and asks if you are Savos. His disembodied voice, often accompanied by a blue wind capable of sapping [[Skyrim:Magicka|magicka]], follows you all the way to the end of the dungeon, where he is found incarcerated by two [[Skyrim:Enthralled Wizard|ex-College thralls]].

Due to the nature of the Staff of Magnus, Morokei elects to use his own spells rather than the staff. This can make him an exceptionally dangerous foe as he can summon a [[Skyrim:Storm Atronach|storm atronach]] in combat and can turn your own summons against you with the spell [[Skyrim:Command Daedra|Command Daedra]]. He is particularly dangerous for players using melee weapons against him because of his [[Skyrim:Lightning Cloak|Lightning Cloak]] spell. He can also use the following spells: [[Skyrim:Greater Ward|Greater Ward]], [[Skyrim:Chain Lightning|Chain Lightning]], [[Skyrim:Thunderbolt|Thunderbolt]], and [[Skyrim:Ebonyflesh|Ebonyflesh]].

